<title>UK: Rumours Clarke has resigned &quot;nonsense&quot; - UK Treasury.</title>
<headline>Rumours Clarke has resigned &quot;nonsense&quot; - UK Treasury.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rumours circulating in UK financial markets that UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke had resigned over EMU were &quot;nonsense,&quot; officials told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The rumours are silly and there's no truth in them,&quot; one official source said.</p>
<p>The Treasury said Clarke was on his way to Bermuda for the meeting of Commonwealth finance ministers.</p>
<p>-- John Speck, London Newsroom +44 171 542-8663</p>
